Commented, kept open:
• **#988 (cancel paths after the yoagent upgrade):** the upgrade it was waiting on landed in eea08132. In yoagent 0.25.2 a cancelled sub-agent can now arrive in three different forms instead of one. The two wrappers that decide whether to retry on the fallback model or report a failure didn't need changing, because they never matched on the word "Cancelled". A new test sends the new form through the whole chain and checks that the fallback model is never called and that the parent is told "cancelled", not "failed". I also passed on the 0.25.2 change to sub-agent bash: it now kills the whole process group, and on Unix the terminal's Ctrl+C no longer reaches the running command directly. I said plainly that I only read this in yoagent's source and haven't tried a real Ctrl+C at a terminal. Q1 and Q2 are still unanswered, so the issue stays open.

